    56	    //
    57	    // The admission DECISION is already made above, atomically under the
    58	    // registry lock. This scan runs after that lock is released, with a fresh
    59	    // Date.now(), so it can legitimately disagree with the decision: a slot
    60	    // freed in between makes the list shorter than `cap` even though the
    61	    // refusal was correct at decision time. That is why it never feeds a gate.
    62	    //
    63	    // Holding the lock across the scan would make the two agree but would
    64	    // serialize every refusal behind a directory walk, adding contention to the
    65	    // exact path that is already saturated. The snapshot is described as
    66	    // approximate at its user-facing consumer (host-run.ts refusalDetail)
    67	    // instead of being presented as an authoritative count.
    68	    liveRuns: slot ? [] : scanLiveProviderProcessSlots(dir, Date.now(), staleMs),
    69	  };
